{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00387 - MONDO_10482",
  "verbalization": "Procyclidine is implicated in the pathogenesis of X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome through a series of indirect but interconnected pathways. The drug is linked to Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism and Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease, both of which are indicated to lead to the target syndrome. This suggests that Procyclidine may exert a role in the development of the syndrome through a mechanism involving the treatment of Parkinson-like conditions. The evidence is supported by the presence of a direct indication to Tolcapone and Istradefylline, which in turn are linked to the syndrome, indicating a potential pathway where Procyclidine may influence the progression or manifestation of the condition through its effects on dopamine-related pathways. The integration of these indications highlights a possible role for Procyclidine in the broader context of Parkinson disease pathology, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
